# Invalid IRIs that percent-encoding CAN repair. `--sanitize-iris` rewrites
# them, the exporter reports `unrepairable=0`, the gate opens, and the
# independent parser must then ACCEPT the result.
#
# This is the case that would catch a referee stricter than the repair. If
# Oxigraph refused a sanitized dump, every dataset in the constellation would be
# unpublishable and the driver would look broken rather than the gate.
#
# One defect per line, one class each: bracket, a second '#', a '%' that is not
# an escape, a raw space.
<http://example.org/ok> <http://example.org/p> "a clean control" .
<http://example.org/a[b]> <http://example.org/p> "bracket outside an IP-literal host" .
<http://example.org/c#d#e> <http://example.org/p> "a second raw '#'" .
<http://example.org/%x-template-artifact> <http://example.org/p> "'%' not followed by two hex digits" .
<http://example.org/a b> <http://example.org/p> "a raw space" .
